---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="assistant - hirn" description="Android mobile companion for hirn desktop.">
  <div class="wrap py-12">
    <a href="/" class="group inline-flex items-center gap-2 mb-8 font-mono text-xs text-secondary hover:text-primary transition-colors">
      <svg class="h-4 w-4 transform transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
        <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M9.707 14.707a1 1 0 01-1.414 0l-4-4a1 1 0 010-1.414l4-4a1 1 0 011.414 1.414L7.414 9H15a1 1 0 110 2H7.414l2.293 2.293a1 1 0 010-1.414z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
      </svg>
      Back to system overview
    </a>

    <section class="mb-12 border-b border-border pb-10">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
        <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-primary text-bg">
          <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <rect x="7" y="2" width="10" height="20" rx="2" />
            <circle cx="12" cy="18" r="1" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,2.75rem)] font-bold tracking-tight">assistant</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xl text-secondary max-w-[680px] leading-relaxed">
        Mobile companion app for hirn desktop. Run tools on the go, keep context available while offline, and sync back whenever your desktop connection is restored.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      <div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-10 order-2 md:order-1">

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Offline-first mobile workflows</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            <strong>assistant</strong> keeps essential project context and task state on-device so you can continue working without a live desktop link. Queue actions locally, review history, and keep moving while traveling.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Desktop handoff and sync</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            When your desktop is reachable again, assistant synchronizes state and queued operations automatically. You can trigger tools from mobile, continue in desktop sessions later, and keep one coherent timeline.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 order-1 md:order-2">
        <div class="p-6 border border-border rounded-xl">
          <h3 class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Android First</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            Current release focus is Android. The companion experience is optimized for quick task execution, context lookup, and desktop handoff.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 border border-border rounded-xl">
          <h3 class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Offline On The Go</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            Key data remains available locally so brief network drops or travel scenarios do not block your workflow.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 border border-border rounded-xl">
          <h3 class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Auto Sync On Reconnect</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            As soon as desktop connectivity returns, assistant syncs messages, state updates, and queued operations automatically.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
